width:161pt;' height='62' width='215'>GNDDENSITY</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Ground Layer Density – A measure of how closed or open the forest floor vegetation cover is within the community. Estimate based on following cover ranges (&lt;10%, 10-25%, 25-35%, 35-60%, &gt;60%).</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>GROUNDSP1</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Seven-character flora code of the most prevalent species within the ground level.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>GNDDOM1</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Ranking of prevalence for the species identified in GROUNDSP1 within the ground level.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>GNDSP1_STA</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>ELC species modifier for GROUNDSP1.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>GROUNDSP2</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Seven-character flora code of the second most prevalent species within the ground level.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>GNDDOM2</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Ranking of prevalence for the species identified in GROUNDSP2 within the ground level.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21