ex (COMPLEX1).</td></tr><tr style='height:31.2pt;' height='42'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:31.2pt; width:161pt;' height='42' width='215'>COMPLEX2</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>4–7-character ELC code describing distinct ELC subunit existing within the larger ELC community. If present.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>COMP2SP1</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Seven-character flora code of the most prevalent species within the complex (COMPLEX2).</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>COMP2SP2</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Seven-character flora code of the second most prevalent species within the complex (COMPLEX2).</td></tr><tr style='height:46.8pt;' height='62'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:46.8pt; width:161pt;' height='62' width='215'>TRAIL_TRMP</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>This can result from pedestrians, mountain bikes, and/or off-leash dogs. Urban forest patches with heavy trampling have virtually no ground layer, except scattered exotics such as garlic mustard. Severity for this and all other disturbances below are discussed in TRCA (2023).</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>BROWSING</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence of herbivory from deer, geese, or other non-domesticated fauna.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>GRAZING</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity of herbivory from cattle or other livestock.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>EXOTICS</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity of the exotic species present in a community, including all layers.</td></tr><tr style='height:31.2pt;' height='42'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:31.2pt; width:161pt;' height='42' width='215'>LOG_CUT</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity&nbsp; of mechanical clearing of the canopy, including opening of the forest for landscaping purposes.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr style='height:31.2pt;' height='42'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:31.2pt; width:161pt;' height='42' width='215'>FLOODING</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity of periodic or permanent flooding conditions, storm-water flooding including scouring, flattened and muddy vegetation and silt deposits.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>BEAVER_ACT</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity of beaver activity.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>TRASH_DMP</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity of litter, illegal dumping, fire-pits, and crude construction.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>FILL_SDMT</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity of soil removal, dumping of fill, or excavation within the community.</td></tr><tr style='height:31.2pt;' height='42'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:31.2pt; width:161pt;' height='42' width='215'>Tree Dieback/Decline</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity of major, widespread tree decline or death from insect outbreak, disease, poisoning, or flooding.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr style='height:31.2pt;' height='42'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:31.2pt; width:161pt;' height='42' width='215'>Storm Damage</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity of sudden tree blow down or breakage due to storm events (usually multiple trees affected in a similar time frame).</td></tr><tr style='height:31.2pt;' height='42'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:31.2pt; width:161pt;' height='42' width='215'>Yard Waste</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence/severity of organic debris dumped from adjacent properties (potted plants, grass and hedge clippings, including potentially live invasive material).</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>VERNAL_PL</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Vernal pool – presence or absence of ephemeral ponds.</td></tr><tr style='height:31.2pt;' height='42'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:31.2pt; width:161pt;' height='42' width='215'>Groundwater Seepage</td><td style='border-left-style:none; border-top-style:none; width:484pt;' width='645'>Presence or absence of groundwater seepage as evidenced by springs, indicator species or iron precipitates.</td></tr><tr style='height:15.6pt;' height='21'><td style='border-top-style:none; height:15.6pt; width:161pt;' height='21' width='215'>ORG_HOR</td>